From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: int3472: 50 ms handshake delay for the ov05c10

On the HP EliteBook X G2i the ov05c10 is powered through an INT3472
handshake pin, which the driver enables with the generic 25 ms delay.
That is not enough for this sensor: the first start after a cold
power-on configures and streams while the part is still coming up, the
ISYS never sees a start-of-frame, and the capture times out. A retry a
couple of seconds later, with the sensor still powered from the failed
attempt, works, which is why the fault looked random and why the
software ISP path, which powers the sensor earlier in its setup, was
never affected.

Intel's ipu6-drivers ships the same change as a blanket bump to 50 ms
(patch/v7.0/0005-platform-x86-int3472-handshake-delay-ov05c10-sensor).
Do it per sensor instead, the way the ov08x40 entry already does.

Superseded upstream by commit 844982d3b993 ("platform/x86: int3472:
Increase handshake GPIO delay to 200 ms"), queued in media-next for
v7.4 with Cc: stable, which raises the default for every handshake
sensor and removes the per-sensor entries. Drop this patch at the next
base bump that contains it. Before that, on a 7.3 base, edd0dd59aca0
("platform: int3472: discrete: Support multiple HIDs per GPIO map
entry") changes the map entry's .hid to a .hids[] array, so the hunk
needs a rebase there. Not submitted upstream.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/next/linux-next.git/commit/?id=844982d3b99340c21dd2125f44e1ad04ace6a38e
Signed-off-by: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c
index 115bb37..42c374f 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c
@@ -164,6 +164,18 @@ static const struct int3472_gpio_map int3472_gpio_map[] = {
 		.con_id = "dvdd",
 		.enable_time_us = 45 * USEC_PER_MSEC,
 	},
+	{	/*
+		 * ov05c10 (HP EliteBook X G2i): the sensor is not ready 25 ms
+		 * after the handshake pin. A cold start that streams straight
+		 * away never delivers a frame; a retry on a still-warm sensor
+		 * does. Intel's ipu6-drivers carries the same 50 ms.
+		 */
+		.hid = "OVTI05C1",
+		.type_from = INT3472_GPIO_TYPE_HANDSHAKE,
+		.type_to = INT3472_GPIO_TYPE_HANDSHAKE,
+		.con_id = "dvdd",
+		.enable_time_us = 50 * USEC_PER_MSEC,
+	},
 };
 
 static void int3472_get_con_id_and_polarity(struct int3472_discrete_device *int3472, u8 *type,
